{
  "dom_id": "step-q169436",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Steven took $6$ days to read a book of $45$ pages. If he read the same number of pages each day, then at what rate did Steven read the book?",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of pages to days is $45:6.$ Expressing this as a fraction, we have:\n\n$$\n\\frac{45}{6}\n$$\n\nWe can reduce this fraction to its lowest terms by dividing the numerator and denominator by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{45÷3}{6÷3}=\\frac{15}{2}\n$$\n\nConsequently, Steven read the book at a rate of $\\frac{15}{2}$ pages per day.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
